/-!
# Prime universe-kernel theory

This is the umbrella import for the conservative Prime universe and outcome
development.  It exposes:

* an exact decidable algebra of universe levels;
* disjoint sealed-Legacy and cumulative-Tower presentations;
* the exact sealed conservativity frontier and its raw-syntax counterexample;
* structural and typed substitution, including context-comprehension laws;
* one declaration-aware typing spine, with proof-carrying signatures,
  monotone extension, exact empty-signature recovery, and a proved
  correspondence to the former declaration calculus;
* the category of declaration-aware well-formed contexts and typed
  substitutions, with constructive terminal empty context, type and term
  reindexing, and the full context-comprehension beta/eta laws;
* a scoped Russell/generated-Tarski presentation boundary, extended by typed
  contextual templates for open families, with the generated grammar proved
  to be exactly the zero-template fragment;
* proof-relevant judgment-indexed computation and conversion evidence, with
  raw declaration equations admitted only through explicit preservation;
* generic open algebraic schemas, parallel reduction, and occurrence-separated
  presentations whose fibre evidence may retain proof-relevant conversion
  receipts; exact nonlinear Prime iota schemas are related conservatively to
  their left-linear occurrence geometry, while the remaining Church--Rosser
  choice is exposed by a machine-checked negative control rather than assumed;
* explicit polymorphic functional composition and Church-list map derivations;
* proof-relevant `Rel` and witness-retaining relational `Chain`, whose
  proof-family interpretation is exactly the GSLT-IL loose-arrow equipment;
* occurrence-bag bind as the engine realization of `Chain`, with truth support
  and evidence-strength loss made explicit;
* level-parametric declaration instantiation, with lookup, typing, and root
  computation transported through one reusable signature operation;
* an intrinsic universe-generic native `List.map` term and a genuinely
  proof-relevant indexed `mapRel` family, including strict positivity, a
  dependent eliminator, and exact typed nil/cons computation receipts;
  on the canonical constructor fragment, actual typed raw elements and
  relation witnesses fold to those intrinsic terms with proved typing and
  are exactly equivalent to the polynomial List/relator semantics;
* the exact native-List representation seam to runtime expression
  `cons-atom`/`decons-atom`, kept separate from the later cost theorem;
* native Peano naturals and length-indexed vectors as a second, genuinely
  indexed realization of the generic positive-family interface, including
  dependent eliminators and proof-relevant iota receipts;
* first-class validated presentation values and relational typed routes, with
  representability as the earned compiled-map license;
* the exact returned-fibre internal-language theorem and its strict
  out-of-image transport boundary;
* an evidence-bearing outcome sum with distinct budget and authority
  refinement axes, and operational faults outside the semantic carrier;
* a strictly-positive, type-valued internal model of authority outcomes,
  runs, receipts, and both refinement witnesses, with exact equivalences to
  the external Lean contracts, together with intrinsic first-class Outcome,
  Run, and provenance-bearing Receipt declarations, dependent eliminators,
  strict-positivity witnesses, exact typed computation receipts, and explicit
  negative recursive-domain controls; a native empty family and first-class
  Authority records retain positive and negative soundness maps, with their
  incompatibility witnessed internally rather than flattened to a Boolean;
  budget and authority refinement are fibres of one intrinsic axis-indexed
  family with ten proof-relevant legal transitions, a dependent eliminator,
  exact computation receipts, exact external fibre models, and mixed histories
  that retain both their intermediate outcomes and the order of improvement;
* the native CeTTa correspondence and occurrence-bag gate obligations; and
* a sound, budget-monotone executable authority on the exact eight-row
  tower-boundary image.

Importing this module supplies theory and proof interfaces only.  It does not
install a native implementation as semantic authority.  The proved
internal-language result is exact on the returned-fibre image; it is not a
claim of semantic-CwF initiality or a universal property for the full command
language.  Those stronger statements remain machine-visible open boundaries.
-/
